1
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:44,359
Laila.

2
00:00:45,039 --> 00:00:46,439
It's a massive escape room complex.

3
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,000
Just the storylines alone,

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,119
there are over a dozen of them.

5
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,320
But all those flashy,

6
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,560
horror elements...

7
00:00:56,039 --> 00:00:57,399
none of that is the point.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,479
When my people were investigating

9
00:00:59,479 --> 00:01:00,759
Li Changyu,

10
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:02,560
they found that under his company's name,

11
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,480
he invested in this escape room business.

12
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,239
Laila,

13
00:01:06,319 --> 00:01:07,519
Li Changyu said earlier

14
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:09,319
that someone incited him to kill.

15
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:10,560
Though there were no explicit instructions,

16
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:11,840
it was deeply manipulative.

17
00:01:13,159 --> 00:01:14,680
I don't know if it's a coincidence,

18
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:15,959
but just in case,

19
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:18,120
we should be extra careful this time.

20
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:22,120
The horror escape room, "Hospital,"

21
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,159
was converted from

22
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:24,359
an abandoned hospital.

23
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,959
I booked the 2:00 p.m. session.

24
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:27,159
As for the plot,

25
00:01:27,159 --> 00:01:28,719
several players wake up

26
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:29,879
to find themselves in a hospital.

27
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,640
There are ten stages in total,

28
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:33,840
and each is said to be harder than the last.

29
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,200
The later ones involve physical challenges.

30
00:01:36,719 --> 00:01:38,239
As long as we clear the first three stages,

31
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:40,159
we'll get a commemorative gold coin.

32
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:42,040
If the later stages

33
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,000
are too tough on my leg,

34
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,200
we can just quit.

35
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:46,000
No problem.

36
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:19,000
This door requires a key to open.

37
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,800
Miss...

38
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,120
Is this your first time playing?

39
00:02:25,199 --> 00:02:27,080
Yeah. I can't walk right now,

40
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:27,879
so I was bored out of my mind

41
00:02:28,199 --> 00:02:29,280
and looking for some fun.

42
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:30,879
My name is Lin Anzhe.

43
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:31,879
You can call me Anzhe.

44
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,639
No worries.

45
00:02:36,919 --> 00:02:38,639
If you ever want to play, Miss,

46
00:02:38,639 --> 00:02:39,800
you can hit me up anytime.

47
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,879
As long as you give me

48
00:02:40,879 --> 00:02:42,280
your contact info once we're out.

49
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,560
We'll talk about that once we're out.

50
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,240
Alright.

51
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:50,599
Thanks, Miss.

52
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,599
Coming out to play in that condition...

53
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:01,599
Aren't you worried about slowing everyone down?

54
00:03:01,879 --> 00:03:03,520
This is a brain game.

55
00:03:04,159 --> 00:03:05,520
All that matters is having the brains for it.

56
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:14,159
Found it.

57
00:03:17,319 --> 00:03:18,800
The key should be in the lockbox.

58
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,159
We just need to crack the code.

59
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:22,960
Decipher the code...

60
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,319
Do we have a time limit in here?

61
00:03:25,439 --> 00:03:26,439
Yes, there is.

62
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,919
If within one hour

63
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:28,879
we haven't cracked it

64
00:03:28,879 --> 00:03:29,840
and can't make progress,

65
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,240
we'll be transferred to the horror room.

66
00:03:31,599 --> 00:03:33,919
Then we can only leave through that exit.

67
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:40,280
Found something.

68
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:42,000
There's a note in the bottle.

69
00:03:47,719 --> 00:03:48,520
Give it to me.

70
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,199
Zero.

71
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,120
Zero.

72
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,439
I found a thermometer here.

73
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:16,240
It reads minus one degree Celsius.

74
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,199
0.

75
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:26,560
1.

76
00:04:26,759 --> 00:04:27,600
3.

77
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:29,920
The code is connected to these numbers.

78
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:37,000
I found something.

79
00:04:37,639 --> 00:04:39,959
R1L3R1L.

80
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,879
What do these numbers and letters mean?

81
00:04:44,759 --> 00:04:46,519
The first symbol is an asterisk.

82
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,240
If the number in the beer bottle is zero,

83
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,879
then it becomes...

84
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,959
0R1L3R1L.

85
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,040
Ignoring the letters,

86
00:04:58,279 --> 00:04:59,879
and looking only at the numbers,

87
00:05:00,319 --> 00:05:02,439
it's 0131.

88
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:04,279
0131.

89
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,920
It's my birthday.

90
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:07,920
And the anniversary of my mom's death.

91
00:05:08,439 --> 00:05:11,959
Is this a coincidence, or by design?

92
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:14,240
R should mean "Right."

93
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,120
L should mean "Left."

94
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,839
Let's try it in the order of this code.

95
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,800
Give it to me.

96
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,879
It actually opened!

97
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:44,600
Did I enter it wrong?

98
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,720
What was the code?

99
00:05:47,399 --> 00:05:49,360
It says "opposite" right there,

100
00:05:49,399 --> 00:05:51,120
which means things are reversed.

101
00:05:51,399 --> 00:05:52,680
In other words, in this section,

102
00:05:52,879 --> 00:05:54,480
everything in this room

103
00:05:54,519 --> 00:05:55,720
could be reversed.

104
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,279
So I entered the previous code in reverse.

105
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,600
Wow, that's amazing!

106
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,480
Pretty amazing, right?

107
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,439
The answer.

108
00:06:39,079 --> 00:06:40,240
Where's the question?

109
00:07:04,839 --> 00:07:06,319
It's Morse code.

110
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:11,160
Isn't this Morse code?

111
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:14,600
Seems like it.

112
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,160
But I don't know how to solve it.

113
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:21,800
I don't get it either.

114
00:07:21,839 --> 00:07:24,399
Guess the last round was pure luck.

115
00:07:24,399 --> 00:07:25,360
Nothing special.

116
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,720
You do it if you're so smart.

117
00:07:28,399 --> 00:07:29,839
You're such a contrarian.

118
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:30,720
No, I'm not.

119
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,600
I don't see you helping out either.

120
00:07:32,839 --> 00:07:34,759
Girl-crazy, snobby suck-up.

121
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:39,920
Miss,

122
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,959
I think you're amazing.

123
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:43,199
I'm sorry.

124
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:46,000
I promised I'd carry you,

125
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:47,720
and now you're carrying me.

126
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,079
Except with this Morse code,

127
00:07:50,079 --> 00:07:51,319
I really don't know

128
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:52,720
how we're supposed to get out.

129
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,759
Clueless?

130
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,519
Go figure it out in the corner, then.

131
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,439
Do you smell that in the air?

132
00:08:06,959 --> 00:08:08,120
Hospital disinfectant?

133
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,560
Phony vibes.

134
00:08:13,199 --> 00:08:15,560
Aren't you a gold-coin player?

135
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,279
Do you really know nothing?

136
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,120
Well, my motives aren't pure.

137
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,720
I want to pursue Miss.

138
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,319
Are you done yet?

139
00:08:26,319 --> 00:08:27,439
Gross.

140
00:08:27,519 --> 00:08:29,000
Can we actually play this escape room?

141
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:54,679
The Morse code puzzle...

142
00:08:54,679 --> 00:08:55,600
I cracked it.

143
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:57,200
"Stethoscope."

144
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,559
It's medical equipment.

145
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,720
The translation is the answer.

146
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,600
You actually know Morse code?

147
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:06,399
Whose girlfriend are you, anyway?

148
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,320
So in Chinese,

149
00:09:10,679 --> 00:09:11,720
it's "stethoscope."

150
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:13,960
In that case,

151
00:09:14,039 --> 00:09:15,279
let's try that answer.

152
00:09:22,159 --> 00:09:23,039
Stethoscope.

153
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,399
Wow.

154
00:09:34,799 --> 00:09:35,679
Miss,

155
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,600
you two are so amazing!

156
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,840
So, are you two a couple?

157
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,639
Hmph.

158
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:46,360
Doesn't look that way to me.

159
00:09:49,159 --> 00:09:49,799
Yeah.

160
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,080
He's my boyfriend.

161
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,600
Doesn't matter.

162
00:09:56,039 --> 00:09:57,360
Even married couples get divorced.

163
00:09:57,519 --> 00:09:59,279
You're only dating right now.

164
00:09:59,519 --> 00:10:00,399
I still have a chance.

165
00:10:00,559 --> 00:10:02,440
Didn't expect that kind of mindset from you.

166
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:06,120
You really have no morals whatsoever.
